§ `Truncated trace default fixture`

-- Review N2 of W8: a trace is cut off at 10000 nodes. `fib 16` fills it before the
-- default is read, so the step that read `the rate` is never reached; the trace must
-- still show the default, once, and not as a line outside the trace.

    GIVEN `the rate` IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
fib n MEANS IF n < 2 THEN n ELSE fib (n MINUS 1) PLUS fib (n MINUS 2)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`big then rate` MEANS fib 16 PLUS `the rate`

#EVALTRACE `big then rate`
